115 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 64 0 R/T(schedules matches on Valorant maps, validates and records match statistics \(kills, deaths and assists\), ranks players on a live leaderboard, calculates rewards and saves the final results to text and CSV files. The project is deliberately built around six core object-oriented programming ideas: classes, inheritance, polymorphism, operator overloading, file handling and exception handling. Two player types, CasualPlayer and ProPlayer, share one virtual interface but score and get rewarded differently, which makes the polymorphism visible in the output. Invalid input such as negative or non-numeric scores is rejected by custom exceptions before it can corrupt the rankings.)/E(schedules matches on Valorant maps, validates and records match statistics \(kills, deaths and assists\), ranks players on a live leaderboard, calculates rewards and saves the final results to text and CSV files. The project is deliberately built around six core object-oriented programming ideas: classes, inheritance, polymorphism, operator overloading, file handling and exception handling. Two player types, CasualPlayer and ProPlayer, share one virtual interface but score and get rewarded differently, which makes the polymorphism visible in the output. Invalid input such as negative or non-numeric scores is rejected by custom exceptions before it can corrupt the rankings.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

