1473 0 obj
<</Title(The same call, p.calculatePoints\(20, 10, 5, true\), returns different values depending on the real type of the object behind the reference. The program output in Section 6 shows this directly: a ProPlayer gets 82.5 points and a CasualPlayer gets 50.0 for identical statistics. Because the functions are virtual, the choice is made at run time. The tournament code contains no if on the player type, so a new category \(for example a StreamerPlayer\) could be added without changing Match or Tournament.)/Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1427 0 R>>
endobj

